217 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 71 0 R/E(Once food is prepared, the next challenge is getting it to the customer efficiently. Delivery partners need to navigate traffic and complete orders within the promised time.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

218 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 71 0 R/E(Routing and scheduling algorithms can determine efficient paths and assign delivery partners based on location and availability. When several orders are placed in the same area, the system can optimise assignments to reduce travel time and distance.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

219 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 71 0 R/E(This is where operations research becomes highly relevant. Problems involving routing, scheduling, assignment and optimisation are not merely theoretical topics studied in an IEM classroom\204they are part of everyday digital services.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

220 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 71 0 R/T(Data: The Invisible Engine)/E(Data: The Invisible Engine)/Pg 13 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

221 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 71 0 R/E(Every order generates information. Platforms can analyse this data to understand customer preferences, identify peak ordering periods, estimate delivery times and improve operational decisions.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

222 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 71 0 R/E(For IEM students, this demonstrates the growing importance of data analytics and decision science. Modern industrial engineers increasingly use data not only to understand what happened, but also to predict what may happen and determine what should be done next.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

223 0 obj
